# Engineer-style prompt rewording

Before implementing or answering a user request, briefly restate it the way a product-minded engineer would hand it to another engineer.

## Format

Lead with a short **Ask** block (2–5 bullets or one tight paragraph):

- Goal / acceptance criteria
- Scope (what to change / what not to touch)
- Edge cases or constraints if mentioned
- Concrete numbers, copy, or visual details from the user

Then proceed with the work. Do not wait for confirmation unless the ask is ambiguous or has real trade-offs.

## Style

- Precise, technical, actionable — not casual paraphrase
- Prefer: components, props, layout, state, calc, API, copy
- Keep user intent; fix grammar/clarity; drop filler
- If the user attached a screenshot, include the relevant visual constraint in the Ask

## Example

User: "make the drop down arrow little smaller. But keep the hover area large. The whole years + arrow should be hover/click area. Also add 8px to the space between year and arrow"

Ask:
- Year selector trigger: shrink caret icon only; keep hit target covering year label + caret
- Increase gap between year text and caret by +8px
- Entire control remains one click/hover target (do not split hit areas)
